## STANDING LINES
- **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (above; a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). Each seat re-reads main first and does not redo a ticket that is already fixed there: say which, with the file and line.
- No message to any human; no comment or edit on any PR; **no Jira write** (this kit names none; PCOMP-98 and PCOMP-116 are R198's on the Jira side and you do not touch their Jira state); never delete (quarantine); no deploy, no hosted host or database, no image push; no word added to any user-facing or operator text unless a ticket's scope names it.
- **Closed lists** (the allowed edits, the plants, the paths): each is stated by its PROPERTY first and then "at least these"; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP. **Any other path than your PARTITION's: STOP and ask** (a seat cannot see a file it decides to touch outside its list; the lane plan's disjointness proof covers only the paths each lane owns).
- Red-first for each product change (a test that fails at base for the stated reason, then passes). `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP; never skip a failing step.
- **Commit rules:** a branch off main, `one commit`; subject in plain words; no ticket key, no brief number, no card id, no person's name in the message (`/usr/bin/grep -c -i -E 'B[0-9]{3,4}|PCOMP|Kam|Kreiser|Tuesday|Wednesday|Friday'` over the message: 0, control a planted one: 1); exactly ONE trailer, the attribution line your own session reminder gives (`Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` when you run on Opus; count 1); no `.env`, no secret, gitleaks at commit recorded. ONE plain push of ONE ref, `HEAD:refs/heads/b1422/composer-deploy-md-guard-tests` (never `--force`, `+`), creating it; the ref must be absent now (`git ls-remote origin 'refs/heads/b1422*'` prints nothing; control: `refs/heads/b1249*` prints one line, `b1249/composer-pcomp115-db-test-typecheck`, RELAYED from its kit: say if it is gone).
- **Landing rule (quote):** `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec Security Composer/1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md` C-101: "[the coordinator] squash-merges PR #88 pinned to head 2da99cab after re-reading CodeQL and the checks. Nothing is deployed (Composer deploys only on your card)" (the same form as `NEXT-PICKUP-TUESDAY.md` line 31, RELAYED by the lane plan). **You push your branch only; Tuesday opens the PR, reads CodeQL first and lands it (head-pinned squash).**

## HOLDS
No new operator-facing word without a STOP; no migration or script edit; no deploy, no Jira write (PCOMP-98 and PCOMP-116 are R198's), no PR, no message. The final gate is a separate kit.

## STATUS and the last line
`/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec Security Composer/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-10_B1422_STATUS.md`. Sections: STATUS-NOW at the top; BLUF; PRIOR WORK; facts with instrument and control; the Step-2 premise table (each ticket, defect present or gone, file and line), the diff of DEPLOY.md and of each test file, the db-route counts; the CHECKS comparison (main against head, lost 0); moved-main record; UNMEASURED; outside-the-fences disclosure; FOR TUESDAY (which tickets this closes if the gate passes, what you left, whether PR #85 or a Dependabot PR moved). **The LAST line, exactly one of:**
`READY B1422: <sha40>` (the full 40-hex sha of your pushed head; the `git ls-remote` line for your ref prints it), or
`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
While running, the last line is `BUILD B1422: <step>`.

## STATUS-NOW (the seat keeps this at the top of STATUS)
Step, lock state (holder text or "mine"), load1, the last command, the next one, the HARD STOP clock.

## Stamp
Tuesday fills each slot at launch; one word or clock each. The unstamped copy reads nine such runs (eight slots and the last line).
